text:
Priya: FYI I opened a PR that modernizes our SDK snippets for streaming + pagination + retries. Preview: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/3582. Biggest change: we standardize on iterator-style reads and add a small retry example for rate limits. Can someone sanity-check wording and edgecases?

Colin: Looked quick. The Python example now uses an async generator which is clearer:```python
async for frame in client.stream_chat(request):
    if frame.status == 'throttle':
        # advisory - caller can backoff and continue
        await asyncio.sleep(backoff())
        continue
    yield frame.content
```
Call out that `status == 'throttle'` is not guaranteed to be present on every provider; treat it as a hint.

Ravi: TypeScript snippet LGTM. We show both streaming and paginated listing for the same resource to avoid confusion:```ts
// streaming chunks
for await (const chunk of client.chat.stream(req)) {
  render(chunk.text)
}

// paginated historical results
let page = await client.history.list({page_token: null})
while (page) {
  page.items.forEach(render)
  page = page.next_token ? await client.history.list({page_token: page.next_token}) : null
}
```
Add one sentence: "Streaming delivers a near-realtime sequence of deltas; pagination returns complete snapshots per page."

Priya: Nice split. Can we also show a tiny language-agnostic backoff pseudocode before the per-SDK samples? Something like:
```
on error if code == RATE_LIMIT:
  wait = min(max_wait, base * 2**attempt)
  sleep(wait)
  retry
```
Helps readers understand it's a caller-level policy versus automatic infra retry.

Colin: For Go I changed the pattern to surface errors on the stream wrapper rather than panic inside the loop:```go
stream, err := client.Stream(ctx, req)
if err != nil { return err }
for {
  resp, ok := stream.Recv()
  if !ok { break }
  if resp.Err != nil {
    // propagate to caller or log and continue
    continue
  }
  process(resp.Data)
}
```
Add note: "respect ctx cancellation and avoid spawning goroutines per stream unless bounded."

Ravi: I found two small phrasing issues in the migration guide: we used the term `cursor` and `page_token` interchangeably. I pushed a tiny patch to the PR clarifying that `cursor` == streaming position (transient) while `page_token` is for pagination (stable).

docs-ci: Docs preview deployed: https://docs-preview.redwood.ai/pr-3582 — build passed :white_check_mark:

Priya: Thanks! Action items: Ravi to add the one-sentence clarifier and the pseudocode block, Colin to add the Go cancellation note, I'll squash and merge after CI green. Ping here if you want a final read. :rocket:
